# Parcego Merchant Dashboard – Sidebar Layout & Navigation Rule

## Objective

Standardize the Merchant Dashboard UI to use a modern sidebar navigation layout, improving usability, clarity, and scalability for future features.

---

## 1. Sidebar Navigation

- **Persistent Sidebar:**  
  - Fixed on the left, always visible on desktop/tablet, collapsible on mobile.
  - Contains navigation buttons for all merchant-accessible pages and subpages.
  - Group navigation items under clear section headings (e.g., "Shipments", "Analytics", "Billing", "Support").
  - Use shadcn/ui components for all navigation elements.
  - Each button must have a unique ID: `parcego-dashboard-nav-btn-[page]`.
  - Section containers must have IDs: `parcego-dashboard-nav-section-[section]`.

- **Role-Based Visibility:**  
  - Only show merchant-relevant navigation items for merchant users.
  - Hide super admin and courier options from the sidebar, but allow direct URL access.
  - Sidebar must be easily extensible for future roles/pages.

- **Accessibility:**  
  - All navigation buttons must be keyboard accessible (tab, enter/space).
  - Use `aria-label` for all nav buttons and section headings.
  - Indicate the current/active page visually and with `aria-current="page"`.

---

## 2. Main Content Area

- **Fluid Container:**  
  - Main content area should fill remaining space, responsive to sidebar state.
  - Use smooth transitions (fade/slide) when switching pages.
  - Container ID: `parcego-dashboard-main-container`.

- **Page Rendering:**  
  - Only one page/component is visible at a time.
  - No full page reloads; use Next.js App Router for navigation.
  - All content must be accessible and responsive.

---

## 3. UI & Styling

- **Design System:**  
  - Use only Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui components.
  - No custom CSS unless absolutely necessary.
  - Follow project-wide naming conventions for IDs and classes (see Naming & Scoping Rules).

- **Transitions:**  
  - Apply premium, subtle transitions for sidebar, nav buttons, and content area.
  - Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for accessibility.

- **Responsiveness:**  
  - Sidebar collapses to a drawer or icon-only mode on mobile.
  - All layouts must be fully responsive and accessible.

---

## 4. Implementation & Refactoring

- **Incremental Refactor:**  
  - Update dashboard pages one by one to fit the new layout.
  - Remove any legacy navigation or layout code.
  - Ensure all navigation flows are tested and accessible.

- **No Backend Changes:**  
  - This rule applies to UI only. Do not modify backend logic, API calls, or business logic.

---

## 5. Example Structure

```jsx
<div id="parcego-dashboard-sidebar" className="...">
  <nav>
    <div id="parcego-dashboard-nav-section-shipments" aria-label="Shipments">
      <button id="parcego-dashboard-nav-btn-shipments" aria-label="Shipments" ...>Shipments</button>
      <button id="parcego-dashboard-nav-btn-create-shipment" aria-label="Create Shipment" ...>Create Shipment</button>
    </div>
    <div id="parcego-dashboard-nav-section-analytics" aria-label="Analytics">
      <button id="parcego-dashboard-nav-btn-analytics" ...>Analytics</button>
    </div>
    <!-- More sections... -->
  </nav>
</div>
<div id="parcego-dashboard-main-container" className="...">
  {/* Render selected page here */}
</div>
```

---

## 6. Enforcement

- All dashboard pages must use this sidebar layout.
- All navigation must be accessible, responsive, and follow naming conventions.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a modern, accessible, and scalable Merchant Dashboard UI with clear, role-based sidebar navigation and a fluid main content area, ready for future enhancements.